cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, or quote a number measured in it, please cite it as below."
title: "See the drone, then hit it (SpeckLock)"
abstract: >-
  Two halves of one problem. Detection: find a drone that occupies 3-14 pixels in 720p
  video from a moving camera, by stabilising and stacking three grayscale moments so that
  the static world cancels and movers leave colour trails — measured on real, hand-labelled
  video. Pursuit: close on that drone with camera-only proportional-navigation guidance,
  a four-camera 360-degree ring and a mission FSM — measured closed-loop in NVIDIA Isaac
  Sim. There is no flight test in this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cherry
    given-names: Nadav
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/NadavCherry/SpeckLock"
url: "https://nadavcherry.github.io/SpeckLock/"
date-released: 2026-08-10
keywords:
  - small-object detection
  - drone detection
  - counter-UAS
  - temporal stacking
  - multi-object tracking
  - proportional navigation
  - Isaac Sim
